From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacky <me@jackyu.cn>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 08:36:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Check the warm-boot mark on t8110 only

The reset path reads the warm-boot mark at 0x2_3D2E_4804, which only the
t8110 runtime's deep-sleep path writes. Under Virtualization.framework
(vresearch1) nothing is mapped at that IPA for a guest with less than about
7.5 GiB of memory: the load takes a synchronous abort before VBAR_EL1 is set,
the framework ends the SEP core with "Unhandled exception code", and the AP's
ROM waits for the mailbox forever. With more memory the IPA is guest RAM, so
a stale 1 there would send a cold boot into the warm path.

Measured on macOS 27.0.1 (26A434) with a vresearch1 build: DFU comes up at
7680 and 8192 MB and never at 4096, 6144 or 7168 MB; with this change it
comes up at 4096 and 6144 MB. Single-stepping the SEP core through the GDB
stub stops at the load, then at the vector offset 0x200.

The vresearch1 build now always starts cold. The t8110 build is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Makefile                  | 3 ++-
 docs/external-contract.md | 9 +++++----
 docs/platforms.md         | 9 ++++++---
 src/runtime/boot/start.S  | 8 ++++++++
 4 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
index b26b822..472133c 100644
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -26,7 +26,8 @@ CFLAGS := --target=aarch64-none-elf -std=c17 -O3 -ffast-math -g \
 	-mbranch-protection=bti -fno-pic -fno-pie -fno-common \
 	-fno-vectorize -fno-slp-vectorize -Wall -Wextra -Werror $(INCLUDES) \
 	-DOPEN_SECURE_ROM_PLATFORM=$(PLATFORM_ID)
-ASFLAGS := --target=aarch64-none-elf -g -c $(INCLUDES)
+ASFLAGS := --target=aarch64-none-elf -g -c $(INCLUDES) \
+	$(if $(filter t8110,$(PLATFORM)),-DOPEN_SECURE_ROM_WARM_BOOT)
 LDFLAGS := -T linker.ld --no-undefined --build-id=none \
 	--fatal-warnings -nostdlib -static
 
diff --git a/docs/external-contract.md b/docs/external-contract.md
index 6144164..c187118 100644
--- a/docs/external-contract.md
+++ b/docs/external-contract.md
@@ -23,10 +23,11 @@ per-platform differences in the handoff are in [platforms.md](platforms.md).
   pointer in x0. On `t8110` it is IPA `0x3_4000_0000`, where the d16
   firmware expects to run (it checks its own PC), so the emulator must alias
   that IPA onto the same memory. See [docs/platforms.md](platforms.md).
-- **Warm boot**: on reset the ROM reads the word at `0x2_3D2E_4804`. If it is
-  `1` (the t8110 runtime's deep-sleep path writes it), the ROM clears it and
-  jumps straight back into the runtime at `0x3_4000_0000`. On a cold boot it
-  must read as anything other than `1`.
+- **Warm boot** (`t8110` only): on reset the ROM reads the word at
+  `0x2_3D2E_4804`. If it is `1` (the t8110 runtime's deep-sleep path writes
+  it), the ROM clears it and jumps straight back into the runtime at
+  `0x3_4000_0000`. On a cold boot it must read as anything other than `1`.
+  The `vresearch1` build does not read it.
 - **DART**: addresses that arrive over the mailbox are dart-sep IOVAs. The ROM
   walks the DART itself (stream 0 at IPA `0x2_5D2C_0000`: TCR at `+0x1000`,
   TTBR at `+0x1400`, two levels of 11 index bits over 16 KiB pages). A
diff --git a/docs/platforms.md b/docs/platforms.md
index 041c956..96cd1d8 100644
--- a/docs/platforms.md
+++ b/docs/platforms.md
@@ -83,9 +83,12 @@ them for this yet (see the end of this page).
 
 ## Not yet covered by the table
 
-- **Warm boot.** On every platform, `start.S` re-enters the runtime at
-  `0x3_4000_0000` when the warm mark at `0x2_3D2E_4804` reads `1`. That is the
-  t8110 behaviour. On `vresearch1` the path has not been exercised.
+- **Warm boot.** Only the `t8110` build checks the warm mark at
+  `0x2_3D2E_4804` and re-enters the runtime at `0x3_4000_0000` when it reads
+  `1`. The `vresearch1` build always starts cold: Virtualization.framework
+  backs nothing at that IPA for a guest with less than about 7.5 GiB of
+  memory, where the load aborts before the vector table is set and the
+  framework stops the SEP core, and for a larger guest it is guest RAM.
 - **Selection at run time.** The row is fixed when the ROM is built. Two ways
   to choose it at run time instead:
   - read the manifest's CHIP/BORD, which the ROM already evaluates;
diff --git a/src/runtime/boot/start.S b/src/runtime/boot/start.S
index eaa1171..469589e 100644
--- a/src/runtime/boot/start.S
+++ b/src/runtime/boot/start.S
@@ -53,7 +53,14 @@ sep_reset_entry:
      * image+0x20000 and returns into the thread that went down (measured on
      * the 22G100 SEP runtime).  A cold boot never has the word
      * set -- only that path writes it -- so nothing else here changes.
+     *
+     * Only t8110 has that path.  Virtualization.framework backs nothing at
+     * this IPA on vresearch1 unless the guest has about 7.5 GiB of memory or
+     * more: below that the load takes a synchronous abort before
+     * VBAR_EL1 is set and the framework ends the SEP core, and above it the
+     * word is guest RAM, which can read 1.
      */
+#if defined(OPEN_SECURE_ROM_WARM_BOOT)
     ldr x10, =SEP_BOOT_WARM_MARK
     ldr w11, [x10]
     cmp w11, #1
@@ -63,6 +70,7 @@ sep_reset_entry:
     isb
     ldr x10, =SEP_BOOT_RUNTIME_ENTRY
     br x10
+#endif
 .Lbootstrap_cold:
 
     adr x10, sep_vector_table
